{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>You shall not bow down to them.</b> Even if others made them." "<b>And you shall not serve them.</b> Even a degrading form of service, since this is how it is worshipped." "<b>For I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> You have a good Master — therefore do not turn to them." "<b>El jealous.</b> Philosophus asked the Rabbi: is a mighty man jealous except of a mighty man, a wise man except of a wise man? The Rabbi said to him: if a person calls his dog by his father's name, is it not logical that his father would be angry with him? He said to him: yes, etc." "<b>Visiting the iniquity of the fathers.</b> Do not read it as 'I will find the transgression.' <b>For I, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the sons</b> — and not because I will exact payment from the son for his father's iniquities, for each man shall die in his own sin; rather, such is the measure: a man sins, HaShem waits for him all his days whether he will repent, and likewise his son and his son's son; but at the fourth generation, if he stands in his fathers' wickedness, HaShem removes him from the world. And this is <b>visiting the iniquity of the fathers</b> etc. — when they are arrayed. How so? A wicked son of a wicked father. [<b>Upon the third and upon the fourth.</b> Such is HaShem's way: to exact payment from a man in the fourth generation to him, as it is written 'upon the third and upon the fourth' — that is, upon the third a little, and upon the fourth — everything — to cut them off from the world.]" "<b>To those who hate Me.</b> If the children hate Me. Now, one might reason: just as the measure of punishment is for four generations, so the measure of goodness is for four generations. Scripture states, ״ועשה חסד לאלפים.״ If it says לאלפים, I might understand only the specific number of two thousand. Scripture states לאלף — generation upon generation, without number and without limit."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:04.126951285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}